Is it just me or is Nethack an all or nothing game?  I took a look at
my scoreboard from version 3.0.7 to 3.0.j(?). (see graph below)
It seems that if I can keep an explorer healthy past about level 5 or so
I have a good chance of making it all the way.  I have only been done in
once with the amulet.  Is this typical or is it a symptom of a hack and
slash mentality?  I find I have very little patience during play so I tend
to fight instead of run.  I have also noticed that a good >45% of my deaths
come from monsters that tend to attack in groups (soilder ants, rothes,
killer bees, orcs).  I am curious to know if others (perhaps, more careful
player's) death function is flatter than mine or is a lot of early deaths
just a feature of the game?

